{
  "timing": "measured",
  "cues": [
    {
      "id": "S001-U001",
      "order": 1,
      "act": "I",
      "speaker": "ORACLE",
      "en": "Well. It's been a while since we used the WISEMAN name.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U001",
      "voice": "alloy",
      "startMs": 5200,
      "endMs": 10600
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U002",
      "order": 2,
      "act": "I",
      "speaker": "ORACLE",
      "en": "We've all been doing our own thing. I think it's time we brought that work back together.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U002",
      "voice": "alloy",
      "startMs": 10760,
      "endMs": 15210
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U003",
      "order": 3,
      "act": "I",
      "speaker": "ORACLE",
      "en": "Let's keep this short. Stick to what we can back up.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U003",
      "voice": "alloy",
      "startMs": 15370,
      "endMs": 18970
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U004",
      "order": 4,
      "act": "I",
      "speaker": "ORACLE",
      "en": "If we're guessing, say so.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U004",
      "voice": "alloy",
      "startMs": 19130,
      "endMs": 21330
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U005",
      "order": 5,
      "act": "I",
      "speaker": "ORACLE",
      "en": "Let's get to work.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U005",
      "voice": "alloy",
      "startMs": 21490,
      "endMs": 23940
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U006",
      "order": 6,
      "act": "I",
      "speaker": "GHOST",
      "en": "Yeah, good to hear you all. I went through Apple's latest disclosures. A couple of things stood out.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U006",
      "voice": "echo",
      "startMs": 24940,
      "endMs": 32390
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U007",
      "order": 7,
      "act": "I",
      "speaker": "ZERO",
      "en": "I've been looking at the ARM64 side. Uh, mostly pointer authentication and how long the objects are supposed to stay alive.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U007",
      "voice": "ash",
      "startMs": 33210,
      "endMs": 43460
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U008",
      "order": 8,
      "act": "I",
      "speaker": "SPECTER",
      "en": "I've been on the browser side. Different surface, but I keep running into some of the same questions.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U008",
      "voice": "coral",
      "startMs": 44280,
      "endMs": 52430
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U009",
      "order": 9,
      "act": "I",
      "speaker": "ROOT",
      "en": "Then let's establish the boundaries first. What do we actually know, and what are we merely assuming?",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": null,
      "voice": null,
      "extraHoldMs": 1935,
      "startMs": 53250,
      "endMs": 59760
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U010",
      "order": 10,
      "act": "I",
      "speaker": "ORACLE",
      "en": "Okay. Ghost, take us through Bluetooth.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U010",
      "voice": "alloy",
      "startMs": 60580,
      "endMs": 64180
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U011",
      "order": 11,
      "act": "II",
      "speaker": "GHOST",
      "en": "Bluetooth was the one that caught my eye.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U011",
      "voice": "echo",
      "startMs": 65000,
      "endMs": 67500
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U012",
      "order": 12,
      "act": "II",
      "speaker": "GHOST",
      "en": "We have reports involving memory corruption, pairing behavior, and insufficient restrictions on authentication attempts.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U012",
      "voice": "echo",
      "startMs": 67660,
      "endMs": 74860
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U013",
      "order": 13,
      "act": "II",
      "speaker": "GHOST",
      "en": "So, three separate issues. Could be three different failure modes.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U013",
      "voice": "echo",
      "startMs": 75020,
      "endMs": 80320
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U014",
      "order": 14,
      "act": "II",
      "speaker": "ORACLE",
      "en": "Do we have anything that actually links them?",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U014",
      "voice": "alloy",
      "startMs": 80670,
      "endMs": 83270
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U015",
      "order": 15,
      "act": "II",
      "speaker": "GHOST",
      "en": "No. Nothing I'd put in a report yet.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U015",
      "voice": "echo",
      "startMs": 83620,
      "endMs": 86820
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U016",
      "order": 16,
      "act": "II",
      "speaker": "GHOST",
      "en": "CVE-2026-113970 is associated with a Bluetooth use-after-free condition.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U016",
      "voice": "echo",
      "startMs": 86980,
      "endMs": 94730
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U017",
      "order": 17,
      "act": "II",
      "speaker": "GHOST",
      "en": "CVE-2026-113965 and CVE-2026-113964 concern pairing-related behavior in CoreUtils.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U017",
      "voice": "echo",
      "startMs": 94890,
      "endMs": 107090
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U018",
      "order": 18,
      "act": "II",
      "speaker": "GHOST",
      "en": "Yeah. Hang on. We don't have enough to call it one chain.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U018",
      "voice": "echo",
      "startMs": 107250,
      "endMs": 111900
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U019",
      "order": 19,
      "act": "II",
      "speaker": "ZERO",
      "en": "Right. It's the same—sorry, no. One's about how long the object stays alive. The other's about what the system trusts.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U019",
      "voice": "ash",
      "startMs": 112250,
      "endMs": 122100
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U020",
      "order": 20,
      "act": "II",
      "speaker": "ZERO",
      "en": "Similar consequences don't imply a common cause.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U020",
      "voice": "ash",
      "startMs": 122260,
      "endMs": 126610
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U021",
      "order": 21,
      "act": "II",
      "speaker": "SPECTER",
      "en": "Wait, can I jump in? Bluetooth and WebKit are different entry points. We should keep those separate for now.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U021",
      "voice": "coral",
      "overlapMs": 250,
      "startMs": 126360,
      "endMs": 133510
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U022",
      "order": 22,
      "act": "II",
      "speaker": "ROOT",
      "en": "The interesting question is whether the security boundary fails before or after the system accepts the external input.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": null,
      "voice": null,
      "extraHoldMs": 2030,
      "startMs": 133860,
      "endMs": 140720
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U023",
      "order": 23,
      "act": "II",
      "speaker": "ROOT",
      "en": "If Bluetooth pairing state is trusted too early, the consequences could be broader than the individual validation failure.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": null,
      "voice": null,
      "extraHoldMs": 2030,
      "startMs": 140880,
      "endMs": 147740
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U024",
      "order": 24,
      "act": "II",
      "speaker": "ROOT",
      "en": "But that's a hypothesis, not a finding.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": null,
      "voice": null,
      "extraHoldMs": 985,
      "startMs": 147900,
      "endMs": 150910
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U025",
      "order": 25,
      "act": "II",
      "speaker": "ORACLE",
      "en": "Yeah. Good. Let's keep that distinction clear.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U025",
      "voice": "alloy",
      "startMs": 151260,
      "endMs": 154660
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U026",
      "order": 26,
      "act": "III",
      "speaker": "ZERO",
      "en": "On ARM64, there's another wrinkle. Pointer authentication.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U026",
      "voice": "ash",
      "startMs": 155010,
      "endMs": 160460
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U027",
      "order": 27,
      "act": "III",
      "speaker": "ZERO",
      "en": "PAC can help detect certain forms of pointer manipulation, but it doesn't guarantee memory safety.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U027",
      "voice": "ash",
      "startMs": 160620,
      "endMs": 167170
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U028",
      "order": 28,
      "act": "III",
      "speaker": "ZERO",
      "en": "You can have a perfectly authenticated pointer to an object that's already gone.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U028",
      "voice": "ash",
      "startMs": 167330,
      "endMs": 172760
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U029",
      "order": 29,
      "act": "III",
      "speaker": "GHOST",
      "en": "Right. The pointer can check out.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U029",
      "voice": "echo",
      "overlapMs": 180,
      "startMs": 172580,
      "endMs": 175380
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U030",
      "order": 30,
      "act": "III",
      "speaker": "GHOST",
      "en": "What I want to know is whether the component still owns the object when it touches it.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U030",
      "voice": "echo",
      "startMs": 175540,
      "endMs": 180790
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U031",
      "order": 31,
      "act": "III",
      "speaker": "SPECTER",
      "en": "We've seen similar reasoning applied to browser memory-safety investigations.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U031",
      "voice": "coral",
      "startMs": 181140,
      "endMs": 186690
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U032",
      "order": 32,
      "act": "III",
      "speaker": "SPECTER",
      "en": "JIT behavior, object lifetime, and state transitions can interact in complicated ways.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U032",
      "voice": "coral",
      "startMs": 186850,
      "endMs": 194000
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U033",
      "order": 33,
      "act": "III",
      "speaker": "SPECTER",
      "en": "I should be clear. That's a parallel in the reasoning. We don't know if the root cause is the same.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U033",
      "voice": "coral",
      "startMs": 194160,
      "endMs": 200010
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U034",
      "order": 34,
      "act": "III",
      "speaker": "ORACLE",
      "en": "Okay, so what would tell us it's an ownership problem? What would we actually see?",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U034",
      "voice": "alloy",
      "startMs": 200360,
      "endMs": 206210
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U035",
      "order": 35,
      "act": "III",
      "speaker": "ZERO",
      "en": "We'd need to see it repeat.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U035",
      "voice": "ash",
      "startMs": 206560,
      "endMs": 209460
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U036",
      "order": 36,
      "act": "III",
      "speaker": "ZERO",
      "en": "We need to identify the object state before the transition, the operation that changes ownership, and the first access that violates the expected lifetime.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U036",
      "voice": "ash",
      "startMs": 209620,
      "endMs": 219520
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U037",
      "order": 37,
      "act": "III",
      "speaker": "ROOT",
      "en": "And we need to avoid mistaking a crash signature for a complete explanation.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": null,
      "voice": null,
      "extraHoldMs": 1555,
      "startMs": 219870,
      "endMs": 224980
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U038",
      "order": 38,
      "act": "III",
      "speaker": "ROOT",
      "en": "A crash tells us where execution failed. It doesn't necessarily tell us where the invariant was first violated.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": null,
      "voice": null,
      "extraHoldMs": 2030,
      "startMs": 225140,
      "endMs": 232000
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U039",
      "order": 39,
      "act": "III",
      "speaker": "GHOST",
      "en": "Yeah, one crash report only gets you so far.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U039",
      "voice": "echo",
      "startMs": 232350,
      "endMs": 237000
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U040",
      "order": 40,
      "act": "III",
      "speaker": "GHOST",
      "en": "You can identify the symptom and still misunderstand the defect.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U040",
      "voice": "echo",
      "startMs": 237160,
      "endMs": 241910
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U041",
      "order": 41,
      "act": "III",
      "speaker": "ORACLE",
      "en": "All right. Let's start with what we can actually observe.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U041",
      "voice": "alloy",
      "startMs": 242260,
      "endMs": 245860
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U042",
      "order": 42,
      "act": "IV",
      "speaker": "ROOT",
      "en": "There's something else.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": null,
      "voice": null,
      "extraHoldMs": 605,
      "startMs": 246210,
      "endMs": 247820
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U043",
      "order": 43,
      "act": "IV",
      "speaker": "ROOT",
      "en": "If the ownership transition happens asynchronously, then the failure may not occur at the point where the object is released.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": null,
      "voice": null,
      "extraHoldMs": 2220,
      "startMs": 247980,
      "endMs": 255540
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U044",
      "order": 44,
      "act": "IV",
      "speaker": "ROOT",
      "en": "The issue isn't necessarily the pointer itself.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": null,
      "voice": null,
      "extraHoldMs": 985,
      "startMs": 255700,
      "endMs": 258710
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U045",
      "order": 45,
      "act": "IV",
      "speaker": "ROOT",
      "en": "It's the assumption that the object remains valid after the ownership boundary changes—",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": null,
      "voice": null,
      "extraHoldMs": 1555,
      "startMs": 258870,
      "endMs": 263980
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U046",
      "order": 46,
      "act": "IV",
      "speaker": "ROOT",
      "en": null,
      "ru": "Нет, подожди... чёрт.",
      "jaPronunciation": "ニェート、パダジー……チョルト。",
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": null,
      "voice": null,
      "startMs": 264680,
      "endMs": 266930
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U047",
      "order": 47,
      "act": "IV",
      "speaker": "ROOT",
      "en": "Sorry. No, wait. Let me put that another way.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": null,
      "voice": null,
      "extraHoldMs": 1175,
      "startMs": 267930,
      "endMs": 271640
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U048",
      "order": 48,
      "act": "IV",
      "speaker": "ORACLE",
      "en": "Mm-hm. Go ahead.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U048",
      "voice": "alloy",
      "startMs": 271990,
      "endMs": 275090
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U049",
      "order": 49,
      "act": "IV",
      "speaker": "ROOT",
      "en": "As I was saying, we need to distinguish memory corruption from a failure in object lifetime management.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": null,
      "voice": null,
      "extraHoldMs": 1935,
      "startMs": 275440,
      "endMs": 281950
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U050",
      "order": 50,
      "act": "IV",
      "speaker": "ROOT",
      "en": "Those are related concepts, but they're not interchangeable.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": null,
      "voice": null,
      "extraHoldMs": 1080,
      "startMs": 282110,
      "endMs": 285470
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U051",
      "order": 51,
      "act": "IV",
      "speaker": "ROOT",
      "en": "Without the execution trace, we cannot establish which condition actually occurred.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": null,
      "voice": null,
      "extraHoldMs": 1365,
      "startMs": 285630,
      "endMs": 290040
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U052",
      "order": 52,
      "act": "IV",
      "speaker": "GHOST",
      "en": "Yeah, we're seeing the same thing on our end.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U052",
      "voice": "echo",
      "startMs": 290390,
      "endMs": 292940
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U053",
      "order": 53,
      "act": "IV",
      "speaker": "GHOST",
      "en": "The available evidence doesn't establish the complete sequence of state transitions.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U053",
      "voice": "echo",
      "startMs": 293100,
      "endMs": 299500
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U054",
      "order": 54,
      "act": "IV",
      "speaker": "ZERO",
      "en": "Okay. Keep going.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U054",
      "voice": "ash",
      "startMs": 299850,
      "endMs": 302450
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U055",
      "order": 55,
      "act": "IV",
      "speaker": "ROOT",
      "en": "Then the next step is straightforward.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": null,
      "voice": null,
      "extraHoldMs": 890,
      "startMs": 302800,
      "endMs": 305460
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U056",
      "order": 56,
      "act": "IV",
      "speaker": "ROOT",
      "en": "Separate the observable failure from the proposed explanation.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": null,
      "voice": null,
      "extraHoldMs": 1080,
      "startMs": 305620,
      "endMs": 308980
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U057",
      "order": 57,
      "act": "IV",
      "speaker": "ROOT",
      "en": "Document the conditions under which the behavior is reproducible, and leave everything else unconfirmed.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": null,
      "voice": null,
      "extraHoldMs": 1650,
      "startMs": 309140,
      "endMs": 314600
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U058",
      "order": 58,
      "act": "V",
      "speaker": "SPECTER",
      "en": "There's one comparison I'd like to make.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U058",
      "voice": "coral",
      "startMs": 314950,
      "endMs": 318250
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U059",
      "order": 59,
      "act": "V",
      "speaker": "SPECTER",
      "en": "On the WebKit side, we've spent years examining how complex state transitions create unexpected memory-safety failures.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U059",
      "voice": "coral",
      "startMs": 318410,
      "endMs": 327260
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U060",
      "order": 60,
      "act": "V",
      "speaker": "SPECTER",
      "en": "Browser engines and Bluetooth services are very different systems.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U060",
      "voice": "coral",
      "startMs": 327420,
      "endMs": 332320
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U061",
      "order": 61,
      "act": "V",
      "speaker": "SPECTER",
      "en": "But the methodology is transferable.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U061",
      "voice": "coral",
      "startMs": 332480,
      "endMs": 335480
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U062",
      "order": 62,
      "act": "V",
      "speaker": "ORACLE",
      "en": "Go on.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U062",
      "voice": "alloy",
      "startMs": 335830,
      "endMs": 336780
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U063",
      "order": 63,
      "act": "V",
      "speaker": "SPECTER",
      "en": "Don't begin by assuming the exploit.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U063",
      "voice": "coral",
      "startMs": 337130,
      "endMs": 340430
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U064",
      "order": 64,
      "act": "V",
      "speaker": "SPECTER",
      "en": "I'd start with the state machine.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U064",
      "voice": "coral",
      "startMs": 340590,
      "endMs": 343740
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U065",
      "order": 65,
      "act": "V",
      "speaker": "SPECTER",
      "en": "Identify which transitions are permitted, which transitions are forbidden, and whether the implementation preserves those constraints.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U065",
      "voice": "coral",
      "startMs": 343900,
      "endMs": 351640
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U066",
      "order": 66,
      "act": "V",
      "speaker": "ZERO",
      "en": "Yeah, same question with pointer authentication.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U066",
      "voice": "ash",
      "overlapMs": 180,
      "startMs": 351460,
      "endMs": 354760
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U067",
      "order": 67,
      "act": "V",
      "speaker": "ZERO",
      "en": "PAC helps. It doesn't tell you the ownership decision was right.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U067",
      "voice": "ash",
      "startMs": 354920,
      "endMs": 359920
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U068",
      "order": 68,
      "act": "V",
      "speaker": "ZERO",
      "en": "If the system makes an invalid ownership decision, an authenticated pointer doesn't make that decision safe.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U068",
      "voice": "ash",
      "startMs": 360080,
      "endMs": 369030
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U069",
      "order": 69,
      "act": "V",
      "speaker": "GHOST",
      "en": "Bluetooth has another piece to it, though.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U069",
      "voice": "echo",
      "startMs": 369380,
      "endMs": 371730
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U070",
      "order": 70,
      "act": "V",
      "speaker": "GHOST",
      "en": "External input, pairing state, authentication restrictions, and privileged processing can all be involved.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U070",
      "voice": "echo",
      "startMs": 371890,
      "endMs": 379490
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U071",
      "order": 71,
      "act": "V",
      "speaker": "GHOST",
      "en": "But we need to know which component actually crosses the trust boundary.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U071",
      "voice": "echo",
      "startMs": 379650,
      "endMs": 383750
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U072",
      "order": 72,
      "act": "V",
      "speaker": "ROOT",
      "en": "That's the distinction I want preserved in the final analysis.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": null,
      "voice": null,
      "extraHoldMs": 1270,
      "startMs": 384100,
      "endMs": 388160
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U073",
      "order": 73,
      "act": "V",
      "speaker": "ROOT",
      "en": "An externally reachable vulnerability is not automatically a remote code execution primitive.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": null,
      "voice": null,
      "extraHoldMs": 1460,
      "startMs": 388320,
      "endMs": 393080
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U074",
      "order": 74,
      "act": "V",
      "speaker": "ROOT",
      "en": "A memory-corruption condition is not automatically an exploitable chain.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": null,
      "voice": null,
      "extraHoldMs": 1175,
      "startMs": 393240,
      "endMs": 396950
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U075",
      "order": 75,
      "act": "V",
      "speaker": "ROOT",
      "en": "And an exploitable condition is not evidence that exploitation has occurred.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": null,
      "voice": null,
      "extraHoldMs": 1365,
      "startMs": 397110,
      "endMs": 401520
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U076",
      "order": 76,
      "act": "V",
      "speaker": "ORACLE",
      "en": "Right.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U076",
      "voice": "alloy",
      "startMs": 401870,
      "endMs": 402420
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U077",
      "order": 77,
      "act": "V",
      "speaker": "ORACLE",
      "en": "It's easy to make the pieces sound like they fit.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U077",
      "voice": "alloy",
      "startMs": 402580,
      "endMs": 405380
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U078",
      "order": 78,
      "act": "V",
      "speaker": "ORACLE",
      "en": "We're here to establish what actually happened.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U078",
      "voice": "alloy",
      "startMs": 405540,
      "endMs": 408440
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U079",
      "order": 79,
      "act": "V",
      "speaker": "ZERO",
      "en": "Then we'll need someone to check it independently.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U079",
      "voice": "ash",
      "startMs": 410440,
      "endMs": 414190
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U080",
      "order": 80,
      "act": "V",
      "speaker": "SPECTER",
      "en": "And say where we ran out of evidence.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U080",
      "voice": "coral",
      "startMs": 414540,
      "endMs": 417190
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U081",
      "order": 81,
      "act": "VI",
      "speaker": "ORACLE",
      "en": "All right. Three tracks. Keep them independent.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U081",
      "voice": "alloy",
      "startMs": 417540,
      "endMs": 421840
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U082",
      "order": 82,
      "act": "VI",
      "speaker": "ORACLE",
      "en": "Ghost, focus on the Bluetooth and CoreUtils disclosures. Establish the documented behavior and identify the unresolved questions.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U082",
      "voice": "alloy",
      "startMs": 422000,
      "endMs": 430500
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U083",
      "order": 83,
      "act": "VI",
      "speaker": "ORACLE",
      "en": "Zero, examine the ARM64 memory-safety implications. I want the pointer authentication assumptions separated from the object-lifetime assumptions.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U083",
      "voice": "alloy",
      "startMs": 430660,
      "endMs": 440710
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U084",
      "order": 84,
      "act": "VI",
      "speaker": "ORACLE",
      "en": "Specter, prepare the WebKit comparison. Methodology only. No implied connection without evidence.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U084",
      "voice": "alloy",
      "startMs": 440870,
      "endMs": 448470
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U085",
      "order": 85,
      "act": "VI",
      "speaker": "GHOST",
      "en": "Yep. I'll take that.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U085",
      "voice": "echo",
      "startMs": 448820,
      "endMs": 450570
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U086",
      "order": 86,
      "act": "VI",
      "speaker": "ZERO",
      "en": "I'll write down what has to hold, and what would make me change my mind.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U086",
      "voice": "ash",
      "startMs": 450920,
      "endMs": 456870
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U087",
      "order": 87,
      "act": "VI",
      "speaker": "SPECTER",
      "en": "I'll keep the browser comparison separate.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U087",
      "voice": "coral",
      "startMs": 457220,
      "endMs": 460620
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U088",
      "order": 88,
      "act": "VI",
      "speaker": "ORACLE",
      "en": "Root, consolidate the findings.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U088",
      "voice": "alloy",
      "startMs": 460970,
      "endMs": 465120
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U089",
      "order": 89,
      "act": "VI",
      "speaker": "ORACLE",
      "en": "No inferred dependencies. No unsupported vulnerability chains.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U089",
      "voice": "alloy",
      "startMs": 465280,
      "endMs": 470180
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U090",
      "order": 90,
      "act": "VI",
      "speaker": "ORACLE",
      "en": "If something cannot be demonstrated, mark it as unconfirmed.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U090",
      "voice": "alloy",
      "startMs": 470340,
      "endMs": 474390
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U091",
      "order": 91,
      "act": "VI",
      "speaker": "ROOT",
      "en": "Understood.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": null,
      "voice": null,
      "extraHoldMs": 415,
      "startMs": 474740,
      "endMs": 476105
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U092",
      "order": 92,
      "act": "VI",
      "speaker": "ROOT",
      "en": "I'll separate verified observations, working hypotheses, and unresolved contradictions.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": null,
      "voice": null,
      "extraHoldMs": 1175,
      "startMs": 476265,
      "endMs": 479975
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U093",
      "order": 93,
      "act": "VI",
      "speaker": "ROOT",
      "en": "Anything without reproducible evidence stays outside the conclusions.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": null,
      "voice": null,
      "extraHoldMs": 1080,
      "startMs": 480135,
      "endMs": 483495
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U094",
      "order": 94,
      "act": "VI",
      "speaker": "ORACLE",
      "en": "Okay. Good.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U094",
      "voice": "alloy",
      "startMs": 483845,
      "endMs": 486395
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U095",
      "order": 95,
      "act": "VI",
      "speaker": "ORACLE",
      "en": "We reconvene when there's something worth examining.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U095",
      "voice": "alloy",
      "startMs": 486555,
      "endMs": 489805
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U096",
      "order": 96,
      "act": "VI",
      "speaker": "ORACLE",
      "en": "Until then, maintain separation between the research tracks.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
      "speaking": true,
      "audioAssetId": "S001-U096",
      "voice": "alloy",
      "startMs": 489965,
      "endMs": 493965
    },
    {
      "id": "S001-U097",
      "order": 97,
      "act": "VII",
      "speaker": "GHOST",
      "en": "Got it.",
      "ru": null,
      "jaPronunciation": null,
